.TH "REQUEST.TEXTSTREAM" "3JS" "September 4, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Request.textStream \- Request: textStream() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]textStream()\f[B]\f[R] method of the \f[CR]Request\f[R]
interface returns a \f[CR]ReadableStream\f[R] that can be used to read
the contents of the request body in chunks of UTF\-8.
.PP
This provides an easier mechanism for streaming the request body than
piping the \f[CR]Request.body\f[R] byte stream through a
\f[CR]TextDecoderStream\f[R].
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] If invoked on a \f[CR]Request\f[R] with a null body, for
example a \f[CR]GET\f[R] request, \f[CR]textStream()\f[R] will return a
valid empty stream.
.RE
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
textStream()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]ReadableStream\f[R].
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
Thrown if the request body is disturbed or locked.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Reading request body content as a text stream
This example shows how to read a request body as a text stream.
.PP
We create a sample \f[CR]Request\f[R], obtain a
\f[CR]ReadableStream\f[R] of its body using \f[CR]textStream()\f[R],
then read the text via a reader created using
\f[CR]ReadableStream.getReader()\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] pElem = document.querySelector(\(dqp\(dq);

\f[B]const\f[R] req = \f[B]new\f[R] Request(\(dqhttps://example.com\(dq, {
  method: \(dqPOST\(dq,
  body: \(aq{\(dqhello\(dq: \(dqworld\(dq}\(aq,
});

\f[B]async\f[R] \f[B]function\f[R] streamRequestText(request) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] textStream = request.textStream();
  \f[I]// instead of\f[R]
  \f[I]// const textStream = request.body.pipeThrough(new TextDecoderStream());\f[R]

  \f[B]const\f[R] reader = textStream.getReader();

  \f[B]while\f[R] (\f[B]true\f[R]) {
    \f[B]const\f[R] { value, done } = \f[B]await\f[R] reader.read();
    \f[B]if\f[R] (done) \f[B]break\f[R];
    pElem.textContent += value;
  }
}

streamRequestText(req);
.EE
